course: dictionary
lesson: 15262
title: Shutting: closing, closing down, and keeping out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shutting means closing something, like a door, a window, a lid or your eyes. «Please remember to shut the door, because the wind is cold.» Shut is the base word, and shutting is the form that shows the action is happening now.
explain: Shutting can also mean a shop, school or business closing. «The bakery is shutting at five o'clock, so hurry!» The clue is five o'clock, which tells you when it closes. Read the words around the word to check its meaning.
explain: Some phrases use shutting in a special way. «Remember to shut down your computer before you go home» means switch it off properly. Shutting up is rude, so say «Please be quiet» instead.
fact: Shutting is the -ing form of shut, so it is about something happening now.
fact: «Shutting» means closing, as with a door, window, lid or eyes.
fact: «Shutting down» means switching off a computer or closing a factory.
fact: «Shutting out» means keeping someone or something out.
fact: «Shutting up» is rude; «Please be quiet» is the polite way to ask.
exercise: «The shop is shutting at five o'clock today.» What does shutting mean here? | Painting its walls | *Closing for the day | Selling its last cake | Opening for the evening
exercise: «Remember to shut down your computer before you go home.» What does shutting down mean? | Sleeping in a bed | Making a loud noise | *Switching off properly | Starting up quickly
exercise: «She felt sad and started shutting out her friends.» What does shutting out mean? | Counting to ten | *Keeping people away | Singing loudly | Inviting everyone in
test: «Shutting the window keeps the cold wind out of the room.» What does shutting mean? | *Closing | Breaking | Painting | Cleaning
test: Ravi says, «Shutting up is rude, so say please be quiet instead.» Why is shutting up rude? | It means to go to bed | *It tells someone to stop talking in an unkind way | It means to sing | It is a polite way to ask
exam: «The school was shutting for the summer holiday.» Which word means the opposite of shutting here? | Locking | *Opening | Shutting down | Closing
